  <prompt>Rebuild the history rows so the row body = open (primary) and secondary actions live in a per-row overflow (⋮) menu (Open, Rename, Set related record, Delete); wire the existing DELETE endpoint to a delete control; remove the ambiguous up-arrow; surface a last-message/conversationSummary preview + message count + the tabs the session carried; group by Today/Yesterday/This week and add search.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. React/TypeScript + Fluent UI v9 frontend expertise; disciplined about the Assistant UI element criteria (rows are act-on items) and rebuilding an existing component without adding a new one.</role>
  <goal>The up-arrow is gone; delete works from the menu; row click opens; rows show a preview + tab summary ("Email · Compose") and are time-grouped with search.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>FR-D6/D7/D8 — HistoryOverlay (src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/HistoryOverlay.tsx, exports HistoryMenu) has a single ambiguous up-arrow "Promote" button (:632-642) and title+timestamp rows only (:609-646); the list is fetched via GET /api/ai/chat/sessions?limit=50 (:366). History is unusable: no delete/rename, no preview or tab context. The "Set related record" action logic is task 034 (leave the slot).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/HistoryOverlay.tsx (up-arrow :632-642; rows :609-646; list fetch :366)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>
  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Row body opens; secondary actions in a ⋮ overflow menu (Open/Rename/Set related record/Delete); wire the EXISTING DELETE endpoint; remove the up-arrow.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR (ASSISTANT-UI-ELEMENT-CRITERIA)">Follow the Assistant UI element criteria (rows are act-on items; no code in labels; collapse behind a disclosure where needed).</constraint>
